sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as MCP client / Codex Hook
    participant MCP as MCP Gateway
    participant Context as Context Engine
    participant SQLite as SQLite WAL
    participant Lance as LanceDB generation
    participant Maint as Maintenance
    participant Infer as Provider or local node

    Client->>MCP: context_supply or memory_recall
    MCP->>Context: request scope (project, call, flow)
    par Canonical facts
        Context->>SQLite: scoped canonical lookup
    and Derived retrieval
        Context->>Lance: query active derived generation
    end
    Context-->>MCP: ranked core / related / divergent context
    MCP-->>Client: bounded context plus audit metadata

    Client->>MCP: capture or derived-work request
    MCP->>SQLite: canonical transaction + durable outbox row
    SQLite-->>MCP: committed request id
    MCP-->>Client: durable admission accepted
    Maint->>SQLite: claim bounded project/config/provider batch
    Maint->>Infer: derived embedding, rerank, or structured work
    Infer-->>Maint: result or explicit failure
    Maint->>SQLite: persist job state, retry reason, reconcile evidence
    Maint->>Lance: update derived projection or shadow generation
    Note over Infer: No SQLite, LanceDB, MCP, or canonical write authority
